   "evidence": "The roadmap target in \u00a75.5 is stated for a closed immersion `i : X \u2192 Y` with ideal `I`, and the later items `normalCone_pullback` and `conormal_regular` will be phrased that way. Every lemma in the file goes through `i.liftCoborder.ker`, and the diff contains no lemma mentioning `i.ker` or `IsClosedImmersion`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/AlgebraicGeometry/NormalCone/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Add an `[IsClosedImmersion i]` lemma, stated as an equality or an isomorphism, giving `i.conormal.obj \u2245 (Scheme.Modules.pullback i).obj i.ker.sheaf` and the analogous statement for `normalConeAlgebra.obj.X n` with `i.ker ^ n`.",
   "issue": "`conormal_obj` and `normalConeAlgebra_obj_X` are stated only in terms of `i.liftCoborder` and `i.liftCoborder.ker` on the open `i.coborderRange`. Nothing identifies them with `(Scheme.Modules.pullback i).obj i.ker.sheaf` (or the n-th power) when `i` is a closed immersion, even though the module docstring says that for a closed immersion `U = Y` and `I` is the ideal sheaf of `X` in `Y`. A consumer holding a closed immersion and its own ideal sheaf cannot rewrite the conormal sheaf without unfolding `liftCoborder`.",
   "line": 135
  }
 ],
